# C11.2: a JDK class is importable by fully qualified name, under both backends.
#
# C11.1 — a class on the *user's* classpath — used to be uncovered because it needs
# a `-cp` flag and `run.py` invoked `java -jar` with no way to add one. That gap is
# closed: `c11_user_classpath.oq` is launched as `java -cp` and imports a class that
# exists only in a fixture jar. This probe stays separate because it checks a
# different thing — that the qualified-name resolution path works on the jar's *own*
# classpath — and merging the two would hide which form resolved the name.
use dev.oqthara.core.Lexer
print Lexer
